-- title:
--   Surjection of localised Hecke algebras for M ∣ M'
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain and is complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $S$ be a set of natural numbers, and let $M, M'$ be nonzero natural numbers with $M \mid M'$, such that weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M')$ satisfy [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure M' 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6), i.e. the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-lattice generated by the forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers is the whole space, and such that every prime divisor of $M'$ belongs to $S$. Here [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) denotes the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$, and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) is the localisation of `heckeBaseAlgebra N S 𝒪` at the image under `latticeBaseChange` of the prime complement of `heckeCharKernel N S 𝒪 θ`, with canonical map [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.π`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L151) from the Hecke algebra. Given ring homomorphisms $\theta$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) and $\theta'$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M' 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$ such that $\theta'(T_\ell) = \theta(T_\ell)$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid M'$ and $\ell \notin S$, the assertion is that there exists an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\Psi$ from [`CuspForm.heckeLocal M' S 𝒪 θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) to [`CuspForm.heckeLocal M S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) which is surjective, which sends the image of $T_\ell$ in the former to the image of $T_\ell$ in the latter for all primes $\ell \nmid M'$ with $\ell \notin S$, and which is universal for this property: for every commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $A$ and all $\mathcal{O}$-algebra maps $f$ on [`CuspForm.heckeLocal M S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) and $g$ on [`CuspForm.heckeLocal M' S 𝒪 θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) with values in $A$ that agree on the images of these $T_\ell$, one has $g = f \circ \Psi$.
--
--   This is the change-of-level (level-lowering) comparison between Hecke algebras localised at a residual eigensystem: away from $S$ and from the primes dividing $M'$ the generators $T_\ell$ at level $M'$ match those at level $M$, and the resulting map of localisations is surjective and determined by its effect on the $T_\ell$. It is used in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algHom_cornerRing_levelLowering_unitRoot_of_degeneracy_level_mul`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algHom_cornerRing_levelLowering_unitRoot_of_degeneracy_level_mul), where the corner-ring and unit-root constructions at level $M'$ are transported to level $M$.
